{{Nihongo|'''Toyozawa'''|豊沢|Toyozawa}} is a metropolis in the [[Miseto region]] of [[Okaiken]]. It is the largest component of the [[Misetogawa]] Metropolitan Area, the [[List of metropolitan areas in Okaiken by population|second largest metropolitan area]] in Okaiken and among the [[List of urban areas by population|largest]] in the world with nearly 12 million inhabitants. Situated at the mouth of the Yodo River on Toyozawa Bay, Toyozawa is Okaiken's [[List of Sanese cities by population|second largest city]] by the daytime population after [[Okami]], and serves as a major economic hub.

Historically a merchant city, Toyozawa has also been known as the {{Nihongo|"nation's kitchen"|天下の台所|tenka no daidokoro}} and served as a center for the rice trade during the [[Honda period]].

